{%- comment -%}
  Local override. Upstream renders one flat list:
      {% bibliography --group_by none --query @*[selected=true]* %}

  Split it into two themed blocks instead. Two explicit queries rather than
  --group_by topic, so the order and the heading wording are both explicit --
  --group_by would sort groups alphabetically and force the heading text to
  equal the raw field value.

  Conditions inside [...] are AND-ed on a comma (bibtex-ruby elements.rb).
  A selected entry with no topic matches neither query and silently
  disappears, so keep topic in sync with selected in papers.bib.
{%- endcomment -%}
<h3 class="topic">Tabular data</h3>
<div class="publications">
  {% bibliography --group_by none --query @*[selected=true, topic=tabular]* %}
</div>

<h3 class="topic">Semantic web</h3>
<div class="publications">
  {% bibliography --group_by none --query @*[selected=true, topic=kg]* %}
</div>
